Derek Ray wrote:
> Jesssica wrote:
> 
>>I'm pretty decent at NetHack.  I've ascended four times
>>with fighting classes.  But whenever I play wizards I
>>never seem to get them past the "killed by a giant bat"
>>stage.  How do you NetHack gurus get wizards to
>>survive, at least until they get Magicbane?  Especially
>>since they can't wear metal armor, so end up having
>>ridiculously high AC...
> 
> Wear the metal armor, hit small things with the staff, and pick up
> daggers from the floor (the Mines are a good source for both).  Throw
> the daggers to soften the bigger things up first.  Engrave Elbereth in
> the dust liberally and early, and throw daggers and/or cast force bolt
> from atop the Elbereth.
> 
> Trying to force the Wizard into the caster role too soon is an excellent
> way to make a miserable splat.  In the early game the only useful spell
> you're guaranteed to have is force bolt, and while it can be nice it
> isn't a substitute for good AC -- your wizard, like most other roles,
> needs to focus mostly on "not being hit" as a path through the early game.

A second opinon; avoid metal armor and use studded leather instead, do
Elbereth, and go for the low level attack spell; as opposed to throwing
daggers (which is in principle a good thing for wizards to do) you won't
erase the engraving if you cast spells. Combine the methods, use dagger
from distance, engrave before monsters are adjacent, use spells while
they are close by. Switch to magic missile spell if you happen to get
that book. As soon as you get Magicbane you have the guaranteed 1 turn
engraving, until then use hard gems to engrave (though do that in time
because it reqires a couple of turns, one turn per letter).

